# 13. Zone Transfer

A DNS zone transfer is a legitimate mechanism for transferring DNS zone information between authoritative servers.

Two important types:

### AXFR

Full zone transfer.

> **AXFR = ALL**

### IXFR

Incremental zone transfer.

> **IXFR = INCREMENTAL**

Unauthorized or improperly restricted zone transfers can expose DNS information.

---

# 14. Subdomain Enumeration

Subdomain enumeration attempts to identify subdomains.

Example:

```text
example.com
     |
     +-- mail.example.com
     |
     +-- portal.example.com
     |
     +-- vpn.example.com
```

### Important

Subdomain enumeration is **one part of DNS/reconnaissance**, not the entire process.

